"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1691,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Isa, narrated to us Abu Mu'awiyah, from Ibrahim al-Hijri, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah (RA), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:

*""Indeed, the prayer that a woman prays, which is most beloved to Allah, is the one she prays in the most secluded part of her house, in a place of darkness.""*

**CHAPTER:**"
1692,"Narrated to us ‘Ali ibn Hujr: Narrated to us ‘Abdullah ibn Ja‘far (may Allah have mercy on him) from his heart: On the authority of Muhammad ibn ‘Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:
“The most beloved prayer for a woman to perform for Allah is that she pray in the darkest, most secluded part of her house.”

**CHAPTER:**"
